WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:09.520
Callie hurried into the community center with her best friend, Allison, trailing after her.

2
00:00:09.521 --> 00:00:14.874
"How did you ever convince me to join Teen Club?" Allison muttered.

3
00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:18.016
"It'll be fun," Callie said.

4
00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:22.867
"And this summer is going to be so much better than last summer.

5
00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:29.853
Remember how we sat around every single day, doing nothing? It was so boring!"

6
00:00:29.854 --> 00:00:41.332
"If you ask me," Allison said, "that's the whole point of summer break—doing nothing."

7
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:45.876
The girls joined some other teenagers sitting in a circle.

8
00:00:45.877 --> 00:00:53.794
The club leader, Sofia, asked everyone to introduce themselves, and then she told them about the club.

9
00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:57.278
"We're going to do lots of activities here in the city.

10
00:00:57.279 --> 00:01:01.920
But we'll also leave the city for some new adventures.

11
00:01:01.921 --> 00:01:05.951
Our first outing is next week, and I'd really like everyone to go.

12
00:01:05.952 --> 00:01:10.644
It will help us get to know each other."

13
00:01:10.645 --> 00:01:17.387
Allison had perked up when Sofia mentioned adventures. "Where are we going?"

14
00:01:17.388 --> 00:01:23.122
"Up to Treetop Mountain for a zip-line ride," Sofia said.

15
00:01:23.123 --> 00:01:25.903
Allison gripped Callie's arm.

16
00:01:25.904 --> 00:01:34.916
"I've always wanted to zip-line," she whispered, "and I heard Treetop's course is awesome!"

17
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:41.647
Callie nodded and forced a smile, but "awesome" wasn't the word that had popped into her mind.

18
00:01:41.648 --> 00:01:45.403
Her word was "terrifying"!

19
00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:50.780
Callie walked home slowly, preoccupied by the outing to Treetop.

20
00:01:50.781 --> 00:01:55.934
"I can't go zip-lining," she thought for the hundredth time.

21
00:01:55.935 --> 00:02:02.396
High places terrified her—she couldn't imagine flying high above trees on a rope!

22
00:02:02.397 --> 00:02:09.430
Nor could she imagine a way to get out of it—Sofia wanted the whole Teen Club to go.

23
00:02:09.431 --> 00:02:16.231
Plus, Allison was really excited, and Callie couldn't bear to let her down.

24
00:02:16.232 --> 00:02:22.007
As Callie approached an apartment building, she put up a hand to shield her eyes from the sun.

25
00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:33.852
"Am I seeing a mirage," she joked, "or is that really Nate Garcia holding a book instead of a game controller?"

26
00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:41.791
"Oh, it's me all right—the new and improved me." Nate rolled his eyes.

27
00:02:41.792 --> 00:02:46.840
"My grades dropped this year, so I've been ordered to do more reading.

28
00:02:46.841 --> 00:02:52.025
And I have to stop hanging out with my friends who play too many video games.

29
00:02:52.026 --> 00:02:54.332
What are you up to this summer?"

30
00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:59.493
Callie told him about Teen Club.

31
00:02:59.494 --> 00:03:03.032
Nate's mother abruptly stuck her head out of a window.

32
00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:11.988
"He'll join that club too. Nate needs to keep busy—and find the right friends!"

33
00:03:11.989 --> 00:03:22.681
The following week Callie found herself staring out the window as the bus climbed the winding road up Treetop Mountain.

34
00:03:22.682 --> 00:03:29.700
The driver parked at the top, and the kids headed over to where Jeff, the guide, was waiting for them.

35
00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:34.589
Callie was trying to calm her nerves, but they weren't cooperating.

36
00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.907
"Who's zip-lined before?" Jeff asked.

37
00:03:37.908 --> 00:03:41.790
Only Nate and another kid raised their hands.

38
00:03:41.791 --> 00:03:47.750
"No problem," Jeff continued, walking over to where the helmets and harnesses were.

39
00:03:47.751 --> 00:03:51.857
"I'm going to demonstrate exactly what to do."

40
00:03:51.858 --> 00:03:57.299
After the lesson, everyone buckled on harnesses and helmets.

41
00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:05.940
Then they walked through the woods until they reached a platform where two zip-lines started.

42
00:04:05.941 --> 00:04:10.465
"When it's your turn, I'll clip your harness to a cable," Jeff said.

43
00:04:10.466 --> 00:04:17.979
"When I say, 'now,' step forward, and keep your legs in front of you."

44
00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:26.677
Soon Allison and Sofia were zooming off, whooping with delight.

45
00:04:26.678 --> 00:04:34.710
Callie stayed at the back of the line, pacing around as her heart pounded and her legs wobbled.

46
00:04:34.711 --> 00:04:40.052
She bent over, desperately trying to remember Jeff's instructions.

47
00:04:40.053 --> 00:04:41.868
"Are you okay?"

48
00:04:41.869 --> 00:04:45.577
Callie straightened up to see Nate gazing at her.

49
00:04:45.578 --> 00:04:53.985
"Not really," she confessed, "because I'm scared—really, really scared!"

50
00:04:53.986 --> 00:04:58.556
"You can do it," Nate said.

51
00:04:58.557 --> 00:05:02.924
Callie shook her head, but Nate kept reassuring her.

52
00:05:02.925 --> 00:05:12.360
"Just remind yourself that zip-lining is fun and safe, and take deep breaths.

53
00:05:12.361 --> 00:05:19.453
I'll be riding on the other zip-line, and afterward you'll be glad you tried it."

54
00:05:19.454 --> 00:05:26.386
Jeff beckoned to Nate and Callie—it was their turn!

55
00:05:26.387 --> 00:05:27.939
Nate took off first.

56
00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:32.598
Callie breathed deeply as Jeff clipped her harness to the cable.

57
00:05:32.599 --> 00:05:37.960
"Now!" he said, and Callie quickly stepped off the platform.

58
00:05:37.961 --> 00:05:44.651
"Whoa!" she cried as she bounded forward. "I'm flying!"

59
00:05:44.652 --> 00:05:49.532
As cool air rushed past, she closed her eyes.

60
00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:57.448
When she opened them again, she gaped at the beautiful expanse spread out in front of her.

61
00:05:57.449 --> 00:06:04.085
Blue sky was everywhere, and below, the trees were a brilliant green canopy.

62
00:06:04.086 --> 00:06:12.924
Allison and the others cheered as Callie reached the other side.

63
00:06:12.925 --> 00:06:18.590
"I did it!" Callie cried, flashing Nate an exhilarated smile.

64
00:06:18.591 --> 00:06:25.304
As he grinned back, a new thought struck her: His eyes were as blue as the sky.

